<https://ontoboard.org/patterns/pmdco-process-temporal-dimensions.owl> rdf:type owl:Ontology ;
                                                                        dcterms:description "Specifies the temporal extent and the temporal boundaries of a process on the time axis. The annealing example gives the process an occupied temporal interval with explicit first and last instants, and names the participants (furnace, ingot)."^^xsd:string ;
                                                                        dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
                                                                        dcterms:title "Temporal dimensions of a process"^^xsd:string ;
                                                                        rdfs:comment """Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK's quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label moved to skos:prefLabel x1; label added x8; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title \"Temporal dimensions of a process\" - the library's name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library's description of the pattern
- header: dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> - https://github.com/materialdigital/core-ontology
Each change is listed under \"curated\" in the pattern's metadata.json in OntoBoard's pattern library."""@en .

